            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p54-q2-c-supplied-answer",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "25.9",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Enter the data values in $x$ and their frequencies in Freq in 1-variable statistics. Read $\\bar{x}=25.9$.\n\nIndependent check: multiplying each $x$ by $f$ gives $216,275,468,0,336$ in row order.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sum f&=9+11+18+0+12\\\\\\sum f&=50\\\\\\sum xf&=216+275+468+0+336\\\\\\sum xf&=1295\\\\\\bar{x}&=\\frac{\\sum xf}{\\sum f}\\\\\\bar{x}&=\\frac{1295}{50}\\\\\\bar{x}&=25.9\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p54-q2-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "Median",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p54-q2-d-supplied-answer",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "26",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "The calculator gives $\\mathrm{med}=26$.\n\nIndependent check: the cumulative frequencies are $9,20,38,38,50$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}n&=50\\\\M_p&=\\frac{50+1}{2}\\\\M_p&=25.5\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe 25th and 26th observations are both $26$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Median}&=\\frac{26+26}{2}\\\\\\text{Median}&=26\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 34
